#Calculate daily water usage in liters.
#######
# Per https://gdchillers.com/resources/data-centers/how-to-calculate-data-center-cooling-requirements-step-by-step 
#We can assume that electricty consumption in IT puts out an equivalent amount of heat. 
#Facility load ranges between 1.05 to 1.15 time for heat generation per source, so you would find IT load, and multiply by 1.1  
# Find IT load per day. 

total_heat_day = SITE_HEAT * (rackcount * SERVERS_PER_RACK * SERVER_CAP * KW_PER_SERVER) * HOURS_PER_DAY * BTUS_PER_KW
total_heat_day

 
